#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Learning outcomes {#learning-outcomes}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This tutorial solves a cardinality-constrained portfolio optimization "
"problem: given the constraint of holding exactly $K$ assets, balance risk, "
"return, and diversification objectives to find the set of optimal "
"portfolios.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "After completing this tutorial, you can expect to understand:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"How to express a portfolio-selection problem with three competing objectives"
" &mdash; low risk, high return, and good diversification &mdash; as a "
"quantum optimization problem.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"How a single QAOA circuit, swept over a set of objective weights, traces out"
" a *Pareto front* of optimal trade-off portfolios.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"How an XY mixer keeps the search inside the \"choose exactly K assets\" "
"subspace, so no penalty term is needed and feasibility is enforced by post-"
"selecting the measured bitstrings.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"How to train the circuit's angles with a matrix-product-state simulator at a"
" scale too large to optimize exactly, following Kotil et al. "
"(arXiv:2503.22797).\n"
msgstr ""

